{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23435 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Eupomatenoid 5 may interact with HuT78, through its targeting of SNU-387, a cell line that is a target of multiple compounds. These compounds—Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, (2-Methyl-5-Prop-1-En-2-Ylcyclohex-2-En-1-Yl) Acetate, and Genipin 1-O-Beta-D-Isomaltoside—share a common target of SNU-387 and, consequently, HuT78. The scores for these paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, suggesting that Eupomatenoid 5 may act through a shared pathway that inhibits SNU-387, which in turn affects HuT78. The recurring involvement of SNU-387 as a target implies that the mechanism may involve the modulation of a cellular process that is critical for the survival or function of HuT78. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Eupomatenoid 5 and HuT78, but further validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction and its biological relevance.",
